#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171870 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172064 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "59f9abf1-17db-5717-8660-a531ef00b15c" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Gamma Function for a Positive Integer"}] :question/id #uuid "62da71f1-5a3a-509a-a68e-0596f88c4ae4" :question/math-academy-id "e-8951" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\Gamma(7)$." :question/worked-solution "For any natural number\n\n$$\nn \\geq 1\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(n) = (n-1)!\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(7) = 6! = 720\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171871 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172065 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c8de43f-dc61-5bbe-8b84-b8aa0be19146" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Gamma Function at a Multiple of One-Half"}] :question/id #uuid "5d084f86-9874-5bdd-a416-dba742d7e4e5" :question/math-academy-id "e-8952" :question/problem "Calculate $\\Gamma \\left(\\dfrac{5}{2} \\right)$." :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(z+1) = z \\Gamma(z), \\qquad \\Gamma \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2} \\right) = \\sqrt{\\pi}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nΓ(\\frac{5}{2}) &= \\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{π} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{π}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171872 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e75041c-d0be-5db2-a0db-7c2c2b57b44e" :knowledge-point/title "Defining the Gamma Function"}] :question/id #uuid "aab1e422-0ac4-59b7-bed9-5ce75b4fe22d" :question/math-academy-id "e-9033" :question/problem "Which of the following integrals are equivalent to $\\Gamma(z)$ for $\\textrm{Re}(z) > 0$?\n\n1. $\\displaystyle \\int_0^1 t^{z-1} e^{-t} \\, \\textrm dt$\n2. $\\displaystyle \\int_0^\\infty \\dfrac{t^{z}}{te^t} \\, \\textrm dt$\n3. $\\displaystyle \\int_0^\\infty \\dfrac{e^t}{t^{1-z}} \\, \\textrm dt$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(z) = \\int_0^\\infty t^{z-1} e^{-t} \\, \\textrm dt, \\qquad \\textrm{Re}(z) > 0\n$$\n\nWith this definition in mind, let's consider each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral I does *not* match the definition. The upper bound of integration does not match that given in the definition.\n- Integral II matches the definition:\n$\\displaystyle \\int_0^\\infty \\dfrac{t^{z}}{te^t} \\, \\textrm dt = \\displaystyle \\int_0^\\infty t^{z-1}e^{-t} \\, \\textrm dt = \\Gamma(z)$\n- Integral III does *not* match the definition. The integrand $\\dfrac{e^t}{t^{1-z}}$ is not equivalent to that shown in the definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172231 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172065 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c8de43f-dc61-5bbe-8b84-b8aa0be19146" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Gamma Function at a Multiple of One-Half"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cef02ecd-9df3-5575-908f-494b203d1b05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{8}\\sqrt{π}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168250} {:answer/id #uuid "4d7da824-7b7d-5f2b-bf06-d3a36b2ae564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{4}\\sqrt{π}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168251} {:answer/id #uuid "56ab95c7-0dfc-5ba0-909f-fc130e29b58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{7}\\sqrt{π}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168252} {:answer/id #uuid "5d4dd217-376e-58fe-9376-6ef1c33bfa6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{8}\\sqrt{π}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168253} {:answer/id #uuid "6f6c8096-4570-5f63-8e7d-61b7819da10e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{6}\\sqrt{π}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168254}] :answer-field/id #uuid "15d1edb6-5522-5f3e-9a34-d393c62a2da0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168249}] :question/id #uuid "985175a0-3817-5f02-8236-9b18519858f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-105737" :question/problem "Evaluate $Γ(\\frac{7}{2})$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172234 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172064 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "59f9abf1-17db-5717-8660-a531ef00b15c" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Gamma Function for a Positive Integer"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8857e53a-b502-56b0-9ed4-9fbfd2a92647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{π}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168268} {:answer/id #uuid "88d1ad98-7c7b-563e-adbc-7215b55c890c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$11$!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168269} {:answer/id #uuid "bfecb03d-1d72-5b71-921a-563166e94e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\sqrt{π}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168270} {:answer/id #uuid "47609bd0-0d60-5e66-97fd-36d0b0f53ff1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$13$!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168271} {:answer/id #uuid "497176c4-b528-51ab-b80b-c99ae7671b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$12$!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168272}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8c9dadc3-3c7d-51dc-ae7b-ace17508786a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168267}] :question/id #uuid "88939e2e-ece9-5768-a030-f015b6